  "id": "Compound::DB00655 - Gene::1544",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Estrone and Cyp1a2, mediated through Estropipate. Estrone is causally linked to several pathological conditions, including Abnormal Withdrawal Bleeding, Superficial Phlebothrombosis, and Retinal Vascular Thrombosis, all of which are caused by Estropipate. Estropipate, in turn, binds to Cyp1a2, indicating a pathway where Estrone may influence Cyp1a2 activity through Estropipate. The low scores in Path 3 (0.54) suggest some uncertainty in the strength of this relationship, but the consistent presence of Estropipate as a mediator across multiple paths supports a mechanistic link. The evidence highlights a potential role for Estrone in modulating Cyp1a2 activity via Estropipate, though further research is needed to confirm the direct interaction and its biological relevance.",
